Error [E-OSTARGET-UNMATCHED-CALL]: `run_paint` uses `LinuxBackend`, whose `impl` is gated to `@Target(Os.Linux)`, without itself being gated to match
  --> tests/ui/os_target_unmatched_call.jet:16:4
    |
 16 | fn run_paint(b: LinuxBackend) -> Int {
    |    ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: an OS-gated impl only exists in the build for that OS; code reachable on other platforms would hit a missing method, so this is caught at compile time, not left to fail as a link (or a raw rustc) error
 Fix: only use `LinuxBackend` from inside an `impl` already gated to `@Target(Os.Linux)`, or move `run_paint`'s body into one
